CORE
main.py
--unwind 75

^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[python-model-bound\.\d+\] .*container capacity exceeded.*: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Appending 70 elements exceeds the verifier's list model bound (64).
The capacity guard reports this as a python-model-bound property
violation instead of silently corrupting state past the array. This
is the sound treatment of the BMC container bound: beyond-capacity
executions are reported (and cut), never silently trusted.
